            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<p>Canada initially led with 60% satisfaction in 1991, significantly higher than the Netherlands at 48%. However, Canada's figure plummeted dramatically to a trough of 19% in 1998, before recovering substantially to 40% by 2007. In contrast, the Netherlands maintained relatively stable levels throughout the period, with figures rising slightly from 48% to 49% in 1998, then declining to 47% in 2007.</p>",
